%N A401683 a(0) = 1; a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} binomial(4*n,k) * a(n-k).
%C A401683 From _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 02 2026: (Start)
%C A401683 In general, for m >= 1, if a(0) = 1, a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} binomial(m*n,k) * a(n-k) then a(n) ~ c(m) * n! * m^n * n^((m-1)*log(2)/(2*m)) / log(2)^n, where c(m) are constants independent of n.
%C A401683 c(1)  = 0.7213475204444817036799623405009460687133... = 1/(2*log(2))
%C A401683 c(2)  = 0.8007252954395988407102111870825109660686692601845218855...
